{"id":901,"date":"2020-11-11T12:33:13","date_gmt":"2020-11-11T20:33:13","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=901"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:08:28","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:08:28","slug":"codrone-arduino-hardware-files","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-hardware-files\/","title":{"rendered":"Installing Hardware Files"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a76803d\" name=\"6a2215a76803d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Preferences<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Open Arduino. If you&#8217;re using Windows, go to File &gt; Preferences. If you&#8217;re using a Mac, go to Arduino &gt; Preferences.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;902&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a768157\" name=\"6a2215a768157\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding link<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]A Preferences window should appear. Find the\u00a0Additional Boards Manager URLs and paste in the URL that&#8217;s below:<\/p>\n<p>https:\/\/raw.githubusercontent.com\/RobolinkInc\/Robolink\/master\/package_rokit_index.json[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;908&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a7681f5\" name=\"6a2215a7681f5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Filter search<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Hit OK to close the Preferences window and go to Tools &gt; Boards &gt; Boards Manager. Find the Type box in the upper lefthand corner, and change the type from All to Contributed.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;909&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a768240\" name=\"6a2215a768240\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Installing<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Find the package &#8220;rokit by ROBOLINK.&#8221; If it says it&#8217;s installed, you&#8217;re finshed! Skip this step! Otherwise, click the package and then click Install.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;911&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a768290\" name=\"6a2215a768290\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Selecting the correct USB driver<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The last thing you need to install is your USB driver for your Smart Inventor Board, which you can get from the Silicon Labs\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.silabs.com\/products\/development-tools\/software\/usb-to-uart-bridge-vcp-drivers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">download page<\/a>. Select your operating system from this page and click &#8220;Download&#8221; under the &#8220;Software&#8221; column. If you are using Mac,\u00a0<strong>skip ahead to step 8.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;914&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a7682da\" name=\"6a2215a7682da\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Extracting package<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Save the file to your desktop. When the file is finished downloading,\u00a0extract\/unzip\/uncompress the file to a new folder, and then run the appropriate \u2018CP210xVCPInstaller_x\u2026exe\u2019 for your operating system.<\/p>\n<p>If you&#8217;re on Windows, you can figure out if you&#8217;re using a x64 or x86 bit operating system\u00a0by going to the start menu, right clicking This PC (or My Computer), and selecting Properties.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;915&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a768327\" name=\"6a2215a768327\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Finalize<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Finally, run the installer. If everything&#8217;s successful, your driver should now be installed!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;916&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215a76838f\" name=\"6a2215a76838f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Mac install for driver<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Once you download the SiLabs USB driver. double click the zip file.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;917&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Open up the DMG file.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;918&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Follow the instructions for the installation window.<\/p>\n<p>Open up the &#8220;<em>Legacy MacVCP Driver<\/em>&#8221; folder, <strong>NOT\u00a0<\/strong>the &#8220;<em>Silicon Labs VCP Driver.pkg<\/em>&#8220;, in this folder.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;919&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Double click on the &#8220;<em>Silicon Labs VCP Driver.pkg<\/em>&#8221; that is inside the &#8220;<em>Legacy MacVCP Driver<\/em>&#8221; folder.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;920&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Follow the installation windows instructions and you will be done.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Preferences [vc_column_text]Open Arduino. If you're using Windows, go to File &gt; Preferences. If you're using a Mac, go to Arduino &gt; Preferences.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=\"902\" img_size=\"medium\" alignment=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-hardware-files\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1752,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2163,2164,2165,2177,2175,2170],"class_list":["post-901","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-hardware","lesson-tag-installation","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/901","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]